"false|true\">value_1</parameter></function></seed:tool_call>\n\n## Important Notes\n- All required parameters must be explicitly provided.\n- The string attribute within the parameter tag specifies the type of the parameter value. For instance, if the value is an integer, number, or boolean, set string=\"false\". If the value is a string, set string=\"true\". Example:\n<parameter name=\"parameter1\" string=\"false\">1</parameter>\n<parameter name=\"parameter1\" string=\"false\">1.0</parameter>\n<parameter name=\"parameter2\" string=\"false\">true</parameter>\n<parameter name=\"parameter3\" string=\"true\">This is a test 1.</parameter>\n- For complex parameter types, such as lists or objects, set string=\"false\" and provide the parameter value in JSON format. Example:\n<parameter name=\"parameter4\" string=\"false\">{\"key1\": \"value1\", \"key2\": \"value2\"}</parameter>\n<parameter name=\"parameter5\" string=\"false\">[1, 2, 3]</parameter>\n\n## Additional Notes\n- Available Apps: [\"com.xianzhiershouwang\"].\n- If you think you have no enough information to complete the task, you should use `clarify` action to ask the user to get more information.\n- If the task involves any risky operations (including sending orders, logging in, etc.), you need to complete them yourself instead of finishing the task."
